// Per-image relaxations for build/gold-images.cs. An image without a rule uses the default:
// no pixel may differ from its golden by 3 or more (the maximum channel difference, alpha ignored).
// A bucket left out of a rule is unlimited. Buckets: "1-2", "3-5", "6-15", "16+".
//
// Relax an image only when its scene cannot be made deterministic, and say why.
[
  // The flock itself is bit-identical run to run (a chaotic system, so any drift would show as the
  // whole flock moving); one pixel at a shadow edge on the ground still flips by ~45 between runs,
  // a rasterisation tie in the shadow map. A handful of stray pixels is allowed for that.
  { "image": "compute-boids", "allow": { "3-5": 20, "6-15": 20, "16+": 20 } }
]
